-# Data duplication and transcription map
-
-## Authority model today
-
-**CURRENT STATE.** There is no single authority for a token/work. Authority is split by consumer:
-
-- chain/TzKT: whether a token exists, active balance, escrow pause, pair storage, operation status;
-- `shared/chain-registry.js`: contracts, endpoints, network labels, explicit ID mirrors;
-- `admin-ui/src/titles/*.json`: Admin-local title authority;
-- numeric files under `admin-ui/src/thumbs/**`: local image/key authority;
-- Webflow CMS: public presentation fields and CMS item identity;
-- `shared/drop-params/drop-params.js`: current configured drop intent;
-- GitHub raw branch copies: deployment/publication parity signal for drop params.
-
-The future record should not replace registry or chain authority. It should own operator-authored work facts and captured integration identities, then derive consumer outputs.
-
-## Duplication map
-
-| Fact | Current sources and destinations | Entered or derived now | Current authority | Recommended future authority | Can generate? | Drift risk |
-|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
-| Collection identity | Registry labels/contracts; title-map filename; thumbnail folder; CMS collection/item `collection`; drop params; DOM list membership | Re-entered/translated | Registry for chain identity; CMS for public label | Authoring `collectionKey` referencing registry-backed collection policy | Yes: contracts, folders, CMS collection ID, labels | Wrong contract, wrong CMS collection, unsafe drop eligibility |
-| Mainnet token ID | Mint result/chain; CMS `token-id`; title-map key; OBJKT URL; drop params | Manually copied | Chain after mint; CMS/local each trust their copy | Captured verified mint result; never typed downstream | Yes | Token/content cross-linking, wrong drop asset |
-| Active-network token ID | Chain; direct IDs or explicit `chainRegistry.testnet.mirrors`; local thumb key; Admin resolution | Derived for HEN/INTRO, assumed identity elsewhere | Explicit registry mirror when present | Registry derivation from canonical mainnet ID; fail if missing | Yes | HEN wrong art/title/pair configuration |
-| Title | Mint metadata (external/untracked); local title JSON; CMS Title and Name; public DOM | Re-entered | Local JSON in Admin; CMS in public site | Canonical authoring record | Yes: local JSON, CMS Title/Name, mint payload | Visible mismatch; wrong operator selection |
-| Artwork source | External authoring file; thumbnail input folder; possibly mint artifact upload | Manually moved | Original file outside modeled repo state | Canonical record references an allowed local source path plus content hash | Yes: derivative jobs | Wrong file minted vs shown in CMS |
-| Local thumbnail key/path | Numeric filename, generated manifest map, audit mapping, CMS image mapping | Inferred from next key / filename | Numeric master filename for Admin | Derive from verified environment token ID and collection asset policy | Yes | Off-by-one or next-ID collision after mint |
-| Thumbnail encoding | Sharp constants and generated JPEG bytes | Derived | Thumbnail tool | Tool/versioned asset profile | Yes | CMS/local visual or performance drift |
-| CMS collection ID | Checked-in schema evidence and historical migration evidence | Manually selected/hard-coded | Remote Webflow schema at execution time | Collection policy plus preflight-confirmed remote ID | Yes after remote verification | Write to wrong collection/site |
-| CMS item ID/locale ID | Remote item and historical migration mapping | Returned by CMS but not generally captured | Webflow | Captured integration result in record/journal | Capture, not derive | Duplicate items, inability to resume/rollback |
-| CMS token-id | Chain ID copied into CMS | Manually entered | Chain should be authoritative, CMS currently independent | Derived from verified mint result | Yes | Wrong route/content identity |
-| CMS Name | Usually duplicates Title | Manually entered in CMS | Webflow | Derived from title unless a collection policy explicitly separates it | Yes | Search/display mismatch |
-| CMS Title | Duplicates local title and often Name | Manually entered | Webflow for public; local JSON for Admin | Canonical authoring title | Yes | Admin/public disagreement |
